 4. 📈 Surprise election rally 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: FactSet. Chart: Axios/Matt Phillips Some of the largest data center operators led a post-election stock rally yesterday — the day after voters delivered a resounding rebuke to data centers themselves, Axios' Emily Peck and Matt Phillips write. 

 Microsoft rose 6.7%, Amazon 6.1%, and Alphabet 3.3%. The big picture: Wall Street is increasingly betting that a slower AI race — and a forced slowdown in spending on the data center buildout — could be good for Big Tech.

