 5. 🤖 AI&#x27;s new charm offensive 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The AI industry is scrambling to repackage a $10 trillion infrastructure buildout to appease a hostile electorate that overwhelmingly voted to restrict data center construction in ballot measures across the country, Axios' Maria Curi writes. 

 Why it matters: Tuesday's election made clear voters won't tolerate unchecked data center growth. To prevent an existential threat, the world's biggest companies are working on a rebrand. Restrictive ballot measures went 43-1 across 10 states, with an average of 75% of voters favoring limits. 

 Analysts expect the backlash to slow — but not stop — the buildout. 🔬 Zoom in: Beyond OpenAI's attempt to rebrand AI data centers as " compute campuses ," companies are offering communities real money, including dividends, benefits for schools or cities, environmental concessions and labor protections.

 Amazon allocated $1 billion to invest in data center communities over five years. Microsoft has a Datacenter Community Pledge. OpenAI today unveiled a Compute Campus Policy Blueprint and outlined tens of millions of dollars in commitments for free school lunches, parks, first responders and other priorities. See OpenAI's new plan ... Share this story ... Get Axios AI+ . 

 
 
